7Uwy0TsbMDfiGChZQ":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.lRXzt7Uwy0TsbMDfiGChZQ","creator":{"__ref":"User:12576884"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1776911719234,"createdAt":1657140798000,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1657220761822,"text":"Rating: 2.5 stars. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003ci\u003eThe Bridge Kingdom\u003c/i\u003e is one of my favorite series, but I’m always a bit hesitant when a series change main characters. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eBut I choose to remain hopeful, because I seriously missed this world and it’s characters. And Jensen writes a good book. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eHowever, I went into this book expecting the story from the previous books to continue. But \u003ci\u003eThe Inadequate Heir\u003c/i\u003e takes place in the same time as \u003ci\u003eThe Traitor Queen\u003c/i\u003e. And I could’ve been fine with that, if I got a new and fresh story, just set during the same time. But the main characters Keris and Zarrah spent the majority of the book in the same place as the previous main characters, Aren. Which made me feel like a read a book I had already read. I already experienced these events, but with characters I liked more. The book didn’t grip me and I didn’t feel excited, because I knew what was going to happen. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI also didn’t really connect with either Zarrah or Keris. They were fine, but not at all as gripping as Lara or Aren. I mean, Zarrah is supposed to be a fierce warrior, but when she realizes she’s been manipulated and lied to her whole life, she rolled over like a kicked puppy. I wanted her to fight back! \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAnd some of the steamy scenes just left me confused. I can’t for the life of me make out the positions they were supposed to be in. Can someone draw me a picture? \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e","rating":3,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1S7KS9TFC0FZ9\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.gGrs_BV_KeOSqz-b\"}}"},"likeCount":33,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":2},"User:21700817":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":21700817,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1702795107i/21700817._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":782,"textReviewsCount":226,"name":"cyra","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/21700817-cyra","contributor":null,"id":21700817},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A3927IA1R101OL":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A3927IA1R101OL"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A3927IA1R101OL\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.WB1aDi44dlXFDh0O\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A3927IA1R101OL","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A3927IA1R101OL"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.WB1aDi44dlXFDh0O","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.WB1aDi44dlXFDh0O"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/21700817?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/4493796650"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.XEwc0T9w3J85xHrHSrNHlQ":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.XEwc0T9w3J85xHrHSrNHlQ","creator":{"__ref":"User:21700817"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1769987439507,"createdAt":1672863149895,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1679040069496,"text":"\u003ci\u003eDrumroll please…\u003c/i\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe award for my least favorite DLJ book goes to The Inadequate Heir!\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThis isn’t necessarily mean that it’s a bad book. I just love Danielle’s books so much that they are usually four or five-star reads for me. Giving one of her books three stars hurt my soul but I have to speak my mind. \u003ci\u003e(This review will have spoilers and they will be tagged so you can still avoid them. Just be mindful that GoodReads app sometimes glitches and show them anyway.)\u003c/i\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eTHE ROMANCE\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThis is more of a preference but I’m a sucker for a slow burn and this book was not it. It wasn’t insta-love but it sure was close to that. They were in love after meeting for a few hours over four nights. This behavior fit Keris, more on that later, but Zarrah? My girl should’ve been better than that. She should’ve been smarter than that.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eTHE REVEAL\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThis is a minor spoiler since we all know they were bound to find out about each other’s identities. My issue was how fast it had happened. Zarrah finds out about Keris’s identity at 30%. I honestly wanted the tension to build up more before this happened so I was disappointed when it happened early on.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eTHE SPICE\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eDanielle used to steer clear from spice so this book having smut caught me off guard not gonna lie. I feel like she started writing smut because BookTok is into it nowadays. Her smut writing skills are top tier, she killed it but it felt weird from time to time just because it felt forced. I believe this book wasn’t written with smut planned in mind so those scenes were added afterward which threw me off the story multiple times.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI especially have a huge issue with one specific spicy scene. \u003cinput type=\"checkbox\" class=\"spoiler__control\" aria-label=\"The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide.\" onchange=\"this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);\" id=\"89943ea3-838b-4f0d-ad95-77d9d75fa256\" /\u003e\u003clabel aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"spoiler\" for=\"89943ea3-838b-4f0d-ad95-77d9d75fa256\"\u003e So Zarrah gets caught and becomes a prisoner of Keris’s father. She makes a revenge plan which will probably get her killed in the end. So to say goodbye to this cruel cruel world, she bangs Keris’s hand out in the open through BARS ON THE FUCKING WINDOW. Let’s put aside the fact that it is impractical and uncomfortable but she jeopardized her lifelong mission and her lover's life to get HAND-BANGED. Keris should’ve used that hand to slap some sense into her because that was not it.\u003c/label\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eTHE “I DON’T HAVE A TITLE FOR THIS BUT I STILL HAVE TO TALK ABOUT IT”\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAside from the spicy scenes that were very unnecessary, there were a lot of missing emotions. Throughout the book, they both lose people who were important and dear to them. \u003cinput type=\"checkbox\" class=\"spoiler__control\" aria-label=\"The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide.\" onchange=\"this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);\" id=\"9da05ba7-e985-4f99-821e-e2ffcdd4f6d4\" /\u003e\u003clabel aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"spoiler\" for=\"9da05ba7-e985-4f99-821e-e2ffcdd4f6d4\"\u003e Zarrah loses her best and only friend and Keris’s only brother who loved him dies.\u003c/label\u003e And yet they were hardly ever phased by those? After they got over the initial shock and feelings, they were just out and about living their lives and were okay? These two were ready to burn the world down for each other but couldn’t care less about other people.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eNow to the characters…\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eKeris, The Horny Heir\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI usually don’t like men and I have a lifelong hatred for Danielle’s MMCs but Keris… Keris! That idiot made me want to scream. Throughout the book, he kept mentioning ideals and lifelong plans to make a better kingdom just to end up like his father, or worse. I may be overreacting a bit since his father was a psychopath with a god complex but hear me out when I say this, Keris can \u003ci\u003eeasily\u003c/i\u003e cross that line for Zarrah. \u003cinput type=\"checkbox\" class=\"spoiler__control\" aria-label=\"The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide.\" onchange=\"this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);\" id=\"1e2fcc7f-564d-4e87-a6f3-ea442ee46045\" /\u003e\u003clabel aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"spoiler\" for=\"1e2fcc7f-564d-4e87-a6f3-ea442ee46045\"\u003e The whole book this asshole was talking about peace and ending the war and saving the innocent and shit like that only to throw it all out and condemn innocent people to their inevitable doom for the sake of Zarrah. And it was against her wishes I might add. I swear to gods, even fictional men can be insufferable. He could’ve respected Zarrah’s choice, the woman he claims he loves, and save a whole kingdom in the process but no. Not to mention the ending! Even when he was a whole king with the power to help his people as he swore he wanted to, he was ready to and will drop everything to go to Zarrah’s aid. His whole thought process goes like this: I am so smart and so strong and I want world peace and I will work for this after I get the pussy. \u003c/label\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eZarrah, The Traitor Queen Remix\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eFalling for the person you were supposed to kill is and always will be fun so the title is a joke. However, I do love how almost all of Danielle’s characters do this. Talk about a favorite trope. I want two things for Zarrah; First I want her to have her revenge on Keris for the burden he had put on her and her life for his own selfish ideas. Second, \u003cinput type=\"checkbox\" class=\"spoiler__control\" aria-label=\"The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide.\" onchange=\"this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);\" id=\"bd58344e-fa5f-472e-8e26-1f54f38feabd\" /\u003e\u003clabel aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"spoiler\" for=\"bd58344e-fa5f-472e-8e26-1f54f38feabd\"\u003e I want her to be FUCKING FREE. She was locked up for the majority of this book when she should’ve been out there fighting and beating ass. Just when she broke free she gets LOCKED UP AGAIN at the end of the book meaning she’ll be a prisoner in the next book either. I am so tired of Zarrah being locked in like a wild animal behind bars and Keris will risk anything and everyone to break her free. Like, give me a break.\u003c/label\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eSo in the end, this is not a bad book. Just not my favorite one especially when I know Danielle can do so much better. Speaking of, y’all should check out her \u003ca href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/41555964-dark-shores\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\"\u003eDark Shores\u003c/a\u003e series because they are elite.","rating":3,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A3927IA1R101OL\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.WB1aDi44dlXFDh0O\"}}"},"likeCount":31,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":5},"User:15643079":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":15643079,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1647504166i/15643079._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":30,"textReviewsCount":354,"name":"J.","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/15643079-j","contributor":null,"id":15643079},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A15JIDQTO29R9D":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A15JIDQTO29R9D"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A15JIDQTO29R9D\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.LOPO06Z4xmN5FwAe\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A15JIDQTO29R9